---
source: crates/roadbook-compiler/tests/fail.rs
---
error[RB0201]: unknown target state `.Missing`: `M.S` has no child `Missing`
  --> RB0201-internal.road:10:15
   |
10 |     on Go -> .Missing
   |               ^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: the children of `M.S` are A

error[RB0201]: unknown target state `.S`: `M.S.A` has no child `S`
  --> RB0201-internal.road:11:27
   |
11 |     state A { on Back -> .S }
   |                           ^
   |
   = help: `.X` names a child of the state the transition is written in; without the dot, `S` is `M.S`, and the transition leaves `M.S.A`

error[RB0201]: unknown target state `.Attempt`: `M.R` has no child `Attempt`
  --> RB0201-internal.road:15:16
   |
15 |       done -> .Attempt
   |                ^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: `.X` names a child of `M.R`; a state with `retry` has none of its own, and the `Attempt` and `Backoff` states the retry compiles to can't be named
